{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading","kind":"remark","title":"Localized knots and hadrons under the knot–particle bijection","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-knot-particle-correspondence","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hadron"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-knot-particle-correspondence","tags":["knot","particle","dictionary","hadron","markov-trace"],"text":"knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading\"></a><p>In particular, the invariant of each localized knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(p, K)</code> in a bundle is a weighted sum over the irreducible summands, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sum_\\lambda y_\\lambda \\chi_\\lambda</code>; no single summand is assigned to it. Hadrons correspond to tensor products of such summands bound by Hopf links.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading.md","heading":"Remark","number":"9.4.7","page":"b/rem-knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading","qa":{"counts":{"pass":43,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":61}}}
